Approval
The creation of an official map is allowed by Wyoming
State Statute §15-1-508 et seq.  The purpose of an official
map is to show locations of collector and arterial streets
which have already been approved or proposed new streets
or street extensions made by the governing body based on a
major street plan.  The placing of any street or street lines
upon the official map does not in itself constitute the opening
or establishment of any street or the taking or acceptance of
any land for street purposes.
